  "instructions": "Cut the onions and separate it as shown\nIn 2 separate bowls prepare the coating\nIn 1st bowl mix oat flour, soy milk, water, salt and pepper to a watery consistency (it should not be 2 watery either)\nIn a separate bowl – mix the breadcrumbs, salt, chilli powder, garlic powder\nNow take each individual slice of the onion, dip in the oat batter, then coat it with breadcrumbs.\nPlace it on a baking tray and bake it at 375F for 10-15 mins – flip it in between",
